<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hunsrück</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hunsrück is a low mountain range in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>, bounded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahe">Nahe</a> and the Saar. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a patchwork of small lordships, among them the counties of Sponheim and Veldenz, the lands of the Wild- and Rhinegraves and the Palatine line of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simmern">Simmern</a>. Its hilly, wooded landscape became widely known through Edgar Reitz's film series Heimat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hunsruck.jpg" alt="Hunsrück" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was ErnstA at German Wikipedia. Later versions were uploaded by Roßbacher at de.wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HunsrueckLage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
